{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Held-out TDD evidence: the full 10-test oracle was RED before implementation (9 new contracts failed for missing behavior; the existing push-only continuity control remained green). The implementer saw only the dirty-tracker happy path. First held-out run found a legacy recovery-state collateral-status gap; one behavior-only redispatch fixed it. Full oracle then passed 10/10, adjacent push suites passed 60/60, and defect-seeded mutations proved both recovery-guard bypass and dirty-commit bypass make their intended tests RED. Restored production is green. Compatibility is additive: push_tickets_branch and its push CLI action remain push-only; legacy trackers receive local lock-artifact exclusions without repository vocabulary/config changes."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786159877293312001,"uuid":"5ebbf4c0-a62b-462d-adcb-7cf5efebcefc"}